---

Review the PR for correctness, completeness, and quality. Try to break it:
trace each changed path and check that the tests would fail if the change were
wrong. Make each finding an inline comment on a changed line with the defect and
the expected behavior.

{{ nitpick_directive }}

Respond to and resolve every earlier review thread whose concern is fixed, and
reply on any you leave open. Do not write pipeline labels. The host applies
`state:implementation-go` or `state:implementation-no-go` from the review
threads left open on the PR.
After `state:implementation-go` is on the PR, arm auto-merge with
`gh pr merge --auto --squash` unless it is already armed. After
`state:implementation-no-go`, run `gh pr merge --disable-auto`. If your sandbox
cannot run `gh`, skip these steps: the host does them.

End with one fenced JSON object:

```json
{"verdict": "GO", "grade": "A", "summary": "...", "comments": [{"path": "...", "line": 1, "severity": "minor", "body": "..."}]}
```

`verdict` is `GO` when the code meets the review criteria, otherwise `NOGO`.
`comments` is free text per finding. `path` and `line` are optional: give them
when you can place the finding on a changed line. A finding you cannot place is
still reported. Use an empty `comments` list when there are no findings.
`grade` is a letter A to F for the whole change. `severity` is `critical`, `major`,
`minor`, or `nitpick`. Both are informational: the host shows them and never blocks on them.
